    originalLanguage: 'French',
    mediumOrFormat: 'Trial defense speech before the criminal jury following the publication of "J’Accuse...!"',
    currentPreservationLocation: 'Bibliothèque Nationale de France, Paris; Journal L’Aurore',
    famousQuote: 'La vérité est en marche et rien ne l’arrêtera! (Truth is on the march, and nothing will stop it!)',
    summary: 'The supreme modern manifesto of intellectual courage against state militarism and antisemitism. Having published his explosive open letter "J’Accuse...!" accusing the French Army General Staff of framing the Jewish captain Alfred Dreyfus, Zola faced criminal libel charges, declaring to the jury that truth will triumph over military cover-ups.',
    historicalContext: 'Captain Alfred Dreyfus was falsely convicted of treason and imprisoned on Devil’s Island. Even after evidence proved Major Esterhazy was the real spy, the military orchestrated a cover-up to protect its reputation. Zola voluntarily risked his career and liberty to force a public trial.',
    fullExcerptText: `Gentlemen of the jury: In the Chamber of Deputies they told you that we were insulting the army. It is a lie! I love the army as a Frenchman; but to love the army does not mean to worship its errors and cover up its crimes!

Dreyfus is innocent; I swear it! I stake my life upon it; I stake my honor upon it! At this solemn moment, before this tribunal which represents human justice, before you, gentlemen of the jury, who are the very embodiment of the nation, before all France, before the whole world, I swear that Dreyfus is innocent!

By all that I have conquered, by the name I have made for myself, by my works which have helped to expand French literature across the world, I swear that Dreyfus is innocent! May all that crumble, may my name perish, if he is not innocent! He is innocent!

Everything seems against me: the two Chambers of Parliament, the civil authority, the military authority, the newspapers with their enormous circulations, the public opinion poisoned by lies! But I am calm, for I have the truth, and truth will conquer!

La vérité est en marche et rien ne l’arrêtera! (Truth is on the march, and nothing will stop it!)`,
